IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `tulrca-types`

-- Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK) — PERIODS,
-- and the s 292A extension for early conciliation.
-- Source: ../registers/source-bundle/ukpga-1992-52.txt.

§ `Periods`

GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, d IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the day` n `days after` d MEANS Date (Day d PLUS n)

-- "the period of N months beginning with" a day ends on the day before the
-- corresponding date, or on the last day of the month where there is none.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x MEANS
    IF   DATE_DAY c EQUALS DATE_DAY x
    THEN `the day before` c
    ELSE c
    WHERE
        c MEANS `add months` x n

§§ `Early conciliation (s 292A)`

-- s 292A(3) "In working out when a time limit set by a relevant provision
-- expires the period beginning with the day after Day A and ending with Day B
-- is not to be counted." Only days within the period the limit counts are
-- stopped: those from the later of the day after Day A and the period's first
-- day, to Day B. If Day A is on or after the last day, (3) adds nothing (F2).
@ref s 292A(3)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, start IS A DATE, e IS AN `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the limit after s 292A(3), from` limit `for a period beginning with` start `with` e MEANS
    IF   e's `Day A` LESS THAN limit AND stopped GREATER THAN 0
    THEN `the day` stopped `days after` limit
    ELSE limit
    WHERE
        first MEANS `the later of` (`the day` 1 `days after` (e's `Day A`)) start
        stopped MEANS Day (e's `Day B`) MINUS Day first PLUS 1

-- s 292A(4) "If a time limit set by a relevant provision would (if not
-- extended by this subsection) expire during the period beginning with Day A
-- and ending one month after Day B, the time limit expires instead at the end
-- of that period."
@ref s 292A(4)
GIVEN limit IS A DATE, e IS AN `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the limit after s 292A(4), from` limit `with` e MEANS
    IF       limit AT LEAST e's `Day A`
         AND limit AT MOST oneMonthAfterB
    THEN oneMonthAfterB
    ELSE limit
    WHERE
        oneMonthAfterB MEANS `add months` (e's `Day B`) 1

@ref s 292A(3)-(4)
@export The last day of a time limit under the Trade Union and Labour Relations (Consolidation) Act 1992 (UK) as extended for ACAS early conciliation by s 292A: the days from the day after Day A to Day B within the period are not counted, and a limit falling between Day A and one month after Day B moves to one month after Day B. DRAFT, not reviewed by a UK lawyer.
GIVEN limit IS A DATE                         @desc The last day of the period before any extension
      start IS A DATE                         @desc The first day of the period
      conciliation IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`  @desc Day A and Day B, if ACAS was contacted
GIVETH A DATE
`the time limit` limit `of the period beginning with` start `extended under s 292A by` conciliation MEANS
    CONSIDER conciliation
    WHEN NOTHING THEN limit
    WHEN JUST e  THEN `the limit after s 292A(4), from` (`the limit after s 292A(3), from` limit `for a period beginning with` start `with` e) `with` e

-- The last day of "N months beginning with" a day, extended by s 292A.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, x IS A DATE, conciliation IS A MAYBE `Early conciliation`
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `months beginning with` x `extended by` conciliation MEANS
    `the time limit` (`the last day of the` n `months beginning with` x) `of the period beginning with` x `extended under s 292A by` conciliation
